      "result": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — the run is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**14 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core browsing, searching, favoriting, and checklist features are well-built. Filtering and search are reactive with accurate counts and a proper no-match state, favorites and saved checklists persist correctly through navigation and reload, and checklist progress aggregates properly to the dashboard.\n\nThe failures cluster into two themes:\n\n**1. Complete absence of input validation on the wedding details form** (CS-8, CS-9, CS-11). The form saves whatever it's given and overwrites good data with bad:\n- Budget accepts `0` and `-5000` → dashboard renders \"$-5,000\"\n- Guest count accepts `-10` and `12.7` → dashboard renders \"Guest Count 12.7\"\n- Wedding date accepts `2020-01-15` → a past date, displayed as the upcoming wedding\n\nEach of these silently destroys the previously saved value, which is the worst-case outcome for a validation gap.\n\n**2. Listing detail views are entirely unimplemented** (IX-12). The \"View Details\" (venues) and \"View Profile\" (vendors) buttons are rendered on all 18 listings but are completely inert — no dialog, no navigation, no DOM mutation at all (body innerHTML byte length identical before and after). Users cannot access any information beyond the card summary.\n\n**One subtler bug worth flagging** (IX-19): Cancel is only half-implemented. The dashboard correctly keeps its saved values, so the bug is invisible at first glance — but the editor's form state is never reset, so reopening it presents the abandoned draft as if it were saved data. A user who cancels, reopens, and clicks Save would unknowingly commit the changes they'd just discarded. This makes it more dangerous than a cosmetic issue, and it compounds with the missing validation above.",
